---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  eyebrow="Legal"
  description={`How ${SITE.name} handles information when you visit the site.`}
  lede="A plain-language summary of the information involved in visiting our site."
  updated="October 14, 2026"
>
  <p>
    This page describes how {SITE.name} handles information when you visit
    <strong>{SITE.url}</strong>. We do not offer accounts, a contact form or an email newsletter.
  </p>

  <h2>Information involved in a visit</h2>
  <p>
    Our hosting provider may process ordinary request information, such as your IP address,
    browser, requested page and time of visit, to deliver the site and keep it working.
    Article images are served from this site's domain. Fonts and other embedded resources may be requested from their providers directly.
  </p>
  <p>
    We do not ask you to submit payment details through this site. If you email us using the
    address on our <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>, we use the information you send to
    respond to your request, not for marketing.
  </p>

  <h2>Advertising and cookies</h2>
  <p>
    Advertising is disabled during the site's editorial review. The site uses Google Analytics to measure visits.
    Google may process information such as your IP address and online identifiers. Analytics may use
    cookies and similar technologies to understand how visitors use the site. We set Google Consent
    Mode defaults to denied; this setting alone is not a consent choice or a substitute for any
    regional consent controls. Read
    <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">how Google uses information from sites that use its services</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
  <p>
    Articles may link to retailers and other websites. Their privacy practices apply once you
    visit them. See our <a href="/disclosure/">disclosure</a> for information about affiliate links.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices and requests</h2>
  <p>
    Depending on where you live, you may have rights concerning personal information held by
    service providers involved in your visit. You can manage advertising preferences through the
    link above and your browser settings. For privacy requests, email the address on our <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We will update this page when the site or its data practices change and revise the date above.
  </p>

</PageLayout>
